{{Quote|A drop of discomfort may be the price of doing business.|Davo Sculdun, to Mon Mothma|<ref name="One Way Out" />}}
'''Davo Sculdun''' was a [[human]]<ref name="One Way Out" /> [[Gender|male]] oligarch,<ref name="Episode Highlights">{{SW|url=news/andor-episode-9-nobodys-listening-highlights|text=''Andor'' Analyzed: 5 Highlights from Episode 9, "Nobody's Listening!"}}</ref> financier,<ref name="223 Fashion">{{InsiderCite|223|Hutt Couture: High Fashion, Star Wars&ndash;Style|Hutt Couture: High Fashion, ''Star Wars''&ndash;Style}}</ref> and [[banker]] from the [[planet]] [[Chandrila]].<ref name="Nobody's Listening" /> Rising to power and wealth through non-conventional means,<ref name="223 Fashion" /> the corrupt<ref name="Mothers Andor">{{SW|url=news/andor-mothers-of-rebellion|text=<i>Andor</i>'s Mothers of the Rebellion}}</ref> Sculdun developed a bad reputation as<ref name="Nobody's Listening" /> a shady<ref name="223 Fashion" /> thug. Much to her upset, [[Tay Kolma]] advised [[Senator]] [[Mon Mothma]] to meet with Sculdun if she wanted to justify the disappearance of 400,000 [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]].<ref name="Nobody's Listening" /> At the [[Chandrilan Embassy]] on [[Coruscant]], Sculdun offered Mothma a loan in exchange for a chance to introduce his son, [[Stekan Sculdun|Stekan]], to the senator's [[Mothma family|daughter]], [[Leida Mothma]]. Mothma said no but Sculdun was convinced that she was thinking the offer over.<ref name="One Way Out" /> Mothma eventually would agree to Sculdun's demands, and she introduced her daughter to his son.<ref name="Rix Road" />

In [[4 BBY]], Sculdun and his wife [[Runai Sculdun|Runai]] attended the [[Marriage|wedding]] of Stekan and Leida on Chandrila at the [[Mothma Estate]]. Sculdun partnered with the curator [[Luthen Rael]]<ref name="OYL">{{Andor|One Year Later}}</ref> in order to bring a rare [[Chandi Merle]] artifact to the ceremonies as a wedding present. Sculdun was central to the many different elements of Chandrilan wedding culture, partaking in the tradition alongside Runai, Mothma, and [[Perrin Fertha]].<ref name="Harvest">{{Andor|Harvest}}</ref>

In [[3 BBY]], Sculdun discovered the [[Coryio Chalice]] in his antiques gallery was a forgery and ordered for the reappraisals of all of his relics<ref name="Friends">{{Andor|I Have Friends Everywhere}}</ref> Sculdun and Runai later hosted a soirée in his accommodation on Coruscant, both Mothma and Fertha were present, and some members of the [[Imperial Security Bureau]] were in attendance. Sculdun gave a handful of guests a tour of his collection, and introduced [[Director]] [[Orson Callan Krennic|Orson Krennic]] to Rael.<ref name="Festive">{{Andor|What a Festive Evening}}</ref>

==Equipment==
The blue gold outfit worn by Davo Sculdun did not quite fit into traditional Chandrilan fashion, signifying his rise to power in a non-traditional manner.<ref name="223 Fashion" />

{{Char-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Sculdun-ConceptArt.jpg|thumb|250px|Concept art for Sculdun by [[Michael Wilkinson]] and [[Andrei Riabovitchev]]]]
Davo Sculdun was mentioned in the [[Nobody's Listening!|ninth episode]] of the [[Andor Season 1|first season]] of the [[Disney+]] television series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]''<ref name="Nobody's Listening" /> which aired on [[November 2]], [[2022]].<ref name="Release dates">{{Twitter|starwars|status/1557442379975573504|[[Star Wars]]|date=2022-8-10|quote=This is what revolution looks like. Watch #Andor, a Star Wars Original Series, streaming only on @DisneyPlus September 21.|archivedate=20220810191942}}</ref> He later made his first appearance in the [[One Way Out|tenth episode]] of the series,<ref name="One Way Out" /> which aired on [[November 9]], 2022,<ref name="Release dates" /> being portrayed by [[Richard Dillane]].<ref name="One Way Out" /> His name was misspelled as "Davos Sculden" in "[[Most Wanted: Cassian Andor and Associates]]," an article written by [[Christopher Cooper]] and published in [[Star Wars Insider 231|''Star Wars Insider'' 231]]<ref name="MWCA&A 231">{{InsiderCite|231|Most Wanted: Cassian Andor and Associates}}</ref> on [[April 29]], [[2025]]<ref name="231 Insider">{{TitanComics|url=m/179-star-wars-insider-231|text=Star Wars Insider #231}}</ref>

Writer [[Dan Gilroy]] believed that Sculdun would own the [[HoloNet News]] and wrote a scene for "[[Welcome to the Rebellion]]" in which he chose to let Mon Mothma's speech against [[Galactic Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]] carry on across the airwaves. While the scene was never realized,<ref name="DanInterview">{{YouTube|video=KeXed1Kozwg|text=Andor S2 Q&A - Dan Gilroy - Episodes 7-9|channel=backstorymagazine2757|name=Backstory Magazine|date=2025-05-07}}</ref> the series did contain a mention of the HoloNews being [[Holo-News buyout|bought-out]] after discussions in Sculdun's office.<ref name="IHFE">{{Andor|I Have Friends Everywhere}}</ref>

